Source of the vendored skill
  The folder skills/reverse-engineer-anything/ comes from the npm tarball
  rea-agents@6.10.1 (integrity sha512-3AWrfFEXppvC98FWhZR2Tzulnqs5xJQrSKmAub6+QME/I58Pr3h8pHqqwM30z2DvlnIx/8Hsu8woMngfi4SNyg==).
  The tarball's SLSA provenance names morluto/rea commit
  8bb01b514ac766c0c3ecc8f362bd38186eaec9c2. At that commit the skill lives in
  .agents/skills/reverse-engineer-anything/. The upstream copy names
  rea-agents@latest; the tarball copy names rea-agents@6.10.1. This pack keeps
  the tarball copy.

Changes made in this pack (MIT permits modification; this notice records them)
  1. SKILL.md front matter: added origin, vetting, vetted, license, upstream and
     upstream-commit. The name, the description and the metadata block are unchanged.
  2. SKILL.md: added the section "Installed by prompt-orchestrator", which names
     the private npm prefix, the MCP server command and the rea-frida set.
  3. SKILL.md: rewrote one sentence about allowed_origins without em dashes.
     The meaning is unchanged.
  4. references/desktop-build.md: harness approval rules override the upstream
     lines on autonomous decisions, the $4 spend default and licence acceptance
     on the user's behalf. The edited lines now defer to the user:
     - "Ask the upfront questions once, then work on your own" now keeps the
       harness approval rules in force during the build.
     - The headless defaults no longer measure tasks within $4. Measuring needs
       a budget that the person names.
     - The agent never accepts a licence itself. The person accepts it, or tells
       the agent to accept that named licence, within the harness approval rules.
     - "Decide everything else yourself" now covers routine build steps only.
     - The Measure section runs only when the requester asked and named a budget.
  The other reference files are byte-identical to the tarball.

Frida (set rea-frida)
